  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukrainian Conflict-related Sexual Violence Integrated Support Mechanism</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contract related to: Ukrainian Conflict-related Sexual Violence Integrated Support Mechanism - This 18-monthexceptional assistance measure will seek to mitigate the disruption of education and psycho-social development in children and provide support to victims of sexual violence in conflict as well as the promotion of their rights at the global level. A first component will focus on the access to education for Ukrainian children by supporting the use of the Ukrainian government&#xbf;s `All-Ukrainian Schools Online Platform&#xbf; and by addressing needs for safe physical learning spaces and materials for children. Comprehensive support will also be given to teachers to continue their work in the on-going crisis situation. Assistance will be specifically tailored to the different situations in the east and west of the country, and also include support to remote education for children who have fled the country, and the facilitation of activities over the summer-months to compensate for lost learning and development opportunities. A second component will focus on assistance to victims of conflict-related sexual violence in conflict in Ukraine. This will include direct assistance to local civil society organisations and first responders as well as specialised investigation teams led by the office of the Prosecutor General of Ukraine.</narrative>
  </description>
